  "details": "Currently the VRC SDK blocks the Build & Publish button if the active unity scene has a avatar present that is not \"publish worthy\".\nThe only way to bypass this is by hiding all avatars before performing the check. However its not uncommon for a unity scene to have a high number of avatars in 1 scene. \nthroughout various updates/sdk's and other changes to avatars over time, the chance atleast one avatar is broken for upload in a big scene is as good as 100%. Though even when the avatar you are intending to upload is all approved, the Build and Publish button remains greyed out.  This makes uploading avatars a slow(er) process as its important to hide all avatars in the scene that are not intended to be uploaded.",
